// The same beat name resolves to a different beat depending on where it is
// written: each parent has its own nested `Local`, and the top-level `Shared`
// is found from everywhere. The resolution stays right when the same names are
// used again and again, from calls, transitions and when insertions. In B's when
// block, its own `true` rule wins the tie: the inserted one was already played.

beat A
  beat Local
    Local of A.
  Local()
  Shared()
  Local()
  when
    + Local
    true
      A has no rule.
  -> B

beat B
  beat Local
    Local of B.
    when
      true
        Rule of B's Local.
  Local()
  Shared()
  when
    + Local
    true
      B has no rule.
  Local()

beat Shared
  Shared beat.

/*
<test>
- expected: |
    ~ Local of A.

    ~ Shared beat.

    ~ Local of A.

    ~ Local of A.

    ~ A has no rule.

    ~ Local of B.

    ~ Rule of B's Local.

    ~ Shared beat.

    ~ Local of B.

    ~ B has no rule.

    ~ Local of B.

    ~ Rule of B's Local.
</test>
*/
